 "about": "Night S1: the words people use to ask for a query, in English, Hinglish and Hindi, mapped to the shared meanings the query writer (app/agents/sqlwrite.py) reasons with. Shared by every database (rule B); the engine only decides the final syntax (LIMIT / TOP / FETCH FIRST). Each 'to' is plain English the writer already reads, so a new language only adds rows here. In 'phrases', {B} and {E} mark a word edge that also works for Devanagari letters (Python's \\b does not).",
